    "narrative": "Our primary offensive catalyst for today\u2019s slate is **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21), who benefits from a prime matchup against Montero. His strong score is fueled by a 14% boost from dynamic platoon splits and a favorable SP xERA of 4.45, positioning him as our most efficient play. Similarly, **James Wood** (74.33) is a core start; while he faces a left-handed pitcher, the matchup against Snelling\u2019s massive 13.50 xERA is an outlier that renders platoon concerns negligible. Batting leadoff, **James Wood** is our highest-upside play for run production. Meanwhile, **Tyler Soderstrom** (61.14) deserves a mention for his favorable park factor, which provides a 16% lift and helps counteract a tougher assignment against Bradish.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros**, whose 40.48 score hovered right at the edge of our efficiency floor. While his park factors and platoon advantages were favorable, he ultimately lacked the ceiling of our starters, and his projection was negatively impacted by a tough matchup against Luzardo. Elsewhere, **Jose Caballero** (39.32) was considered but ultimately fell below our 40-point threshold, as his platoon disadvantage against Misiorowski proved too detrimental to his SB-heavy profile. We also continue to monitor the status of **Giancarlo Stanton**, who remains sidelined on the IL, limiting our depth in power-heavy slots.\n\nWe are exercising caution with several high-profile starters due to elite pitching matchups. **Corbin Carroll** (58.71) and **Gabriel Moreno** (42.12) are both facing McLean, whose 2.93 xERA significantly dampens their projected output. Despite these tough conditions, **Corbin Carroll** remains a start due to his speed profile and order placement, but his efficiency score reflects the underlying risk. **Travis Bazzana** was excluded not only due to his poor platoon split against Prielipp but also because of a 42% rain risk in his contest, providing a clear signal to keep him on the bench to preserve our limited game caps.",
